WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.960
Night.

2
00:00:01.010 --> 00:00:02.700
A masked dance.

3
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:03.870
A garden.

4
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:05.740
A window at dawn.

5
00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:07.820
A tomb by torchlight.

6
00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:12.850
In every scene, one small point
of light glows against the dark.

7
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:16.050
When Romeo first sees Juliet, he says, "O,

8
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:19.330
she doth teach the
torches to burn bright!"

9
00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.600
Their love lives in the dark.

10
00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:24.390
So why is it always described in light?

11
00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:27.510
In this mission, you'll hear
the beat of the play's verse,

12
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.520
and spot where it slips
into prose and rhyme.

13
00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:33.320
You'll take apart Romeo's
first sight of Juliet,

14
00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:34.820
image by image.

15
00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:38.000
And you'll track light and
dark right through the play,

16
00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:40.180
from the balcony to the tomb.

17
00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:44.140
Your mission: explain why
their love is always light.
